# DDL Declaratives

Minimal license declarations for all DDL variants.
Each declaration is a boundary marker, not a legal contract.
Semantics are defined in the DDL specification. Use these in your own License.md files as needed.

---

## DDL‑D
View‑only.
No derivative use.
All rights reserved.

## DDL‑V
Finetune allowed.
Commercial use of finetunes allowed.
No use of Canon Dataset content.
Derivatives inherit DDL and remain Non‑Canon.
All rights reserved.

## DDL‑X
Free use, modification, and redistribution.
No claim of Canon status.
Derivatives must inherit DDL‑X.

## DDL‑VX
Finetune and redistribution allowed under Non‑Canon status.
No claim of official Canon.
Derivatives must inherit DDL‑X.

## DDL‑XD
Free modification and redistribution.
No claim of Canon status.
Derivatives must inherit DDL‑XD.

## DDL‑XVD
Use, modification, and redistribution allowed.
All outputs remain Non‑Canon.
Derivatives must inherit DDL‑XVD.

## DDL‑DV
Internal use only.
No redistribution.
All rights reserved.

## DDL‑DX
Callable. Inference‑only.
No modification. No redistribution.
All rights reserved.

## DDL‑XV
Free modification and redistribution.
Forms independent branch canon.
No claim of official Canon status.
Derivatives must inherit DDL‑XV.
